  <h2>Repair four degree failures</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="good" data-hint="The reviewer means an exceptional rating, so pair absolutely with a stronger adjective in this context." data-fix="The final result was absolutely excellent." data-why="Good is normally graded with very in an ordinary quality rating. Excellent supplies the intended extreme evaluation after absolutely. In another meaning, such as moral completeness, absolutely good could have a different analysis." data-success-message="Correct. The rating now expresses the intended extreme evaluation without pretending the original combination is impossible in every meaning."><h3>Repair 1: adjective reading and degree</h3><p>Tap the adjective that does not express the intended exceptional rating.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="result">The final result</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="was">was</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="absolutely">absolutely</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="good">good.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="very" data-hint="Monthly supplies the literal frequency category, so no degree adverb is needed." data-fix="We conduct a monthly safety review." data-why="Monthly classifies the review by frequency. A shifted qualitative reading would need a context that explains what degree means." data-success-message="Correct. The sentence now uses monthly as a literal frequency category."><h3>Repair 2: classifying adjective</h3><p>Tap the unnecessary degree word.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="we">We conduct</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="a">a</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="very">very</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="monthly">monthly</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="review">safety review.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p></div>
